## Usage

The current pinned native artifact is loaded below with the repository preprocessing (256×256, [0,1], no ImageNet normalization). The exported processor has a different configuration and is bypassed; this example does not verify the legacy metrics. When publishing a new model revision, update the pinned SHA with its actual provenance.


```python
import numpy as np
import torch
from PIL import Image
from torchvision.transforms import v2
from transformers import AutoModelForSemanticSegmentation

model = AutoModelForSemanticSegmentation.from_pretrained(
    "{{ repo_id }}",
    revision="0ea834ffd86dbca24666b34fa358387ec86f4bdf",
    use_safetensors=True, trust_remote_code=False,
).eval()
image = Image.open("slice.tif").convert("RGB")
pixels = torch.from_numpy(np.asarray(image, dtype=np.float32) / 255.0).permute(2, 0, 1)
pixels = v2.Resize((256, 256), antialias=True)(pixels).unsqueeze(0)
with torch.inference_mode():
    logits = model(pixel_values=pixels).logits
    logits = torch.nn.functional.interpolate(
        logits, size=(256, 256), mode="bilinear", align_corners=False
    )
    mask = logits.argmax(dim=1)[0]  # 256 x 256; 0 background, 1 tumor
```


